###  FEMA NRI-specific measuredProperties
Node: dcid:femaSocialVulnerability
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "femaSocialVulnerability"
description: "The susceptibility of social groups to the adverse impacts of natural hazards,including disproportionate death,injury,loss,or disruption of livelihood. This is a measure defined and computed by the US Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)."
descriptionUrl: "https://hazards.fema.gov/nri/social-vulnerability"
domainIncludes: dcid:NaturalHazardImpact

Node: dcid:femaCommunityResilience
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "femaCommunityResilience"
description: "The ability of a community to prepare for anticipated natural hazards,adapt to changing conditions,and withstand and recover rapidly from disruptions. This is a measure defined and computed by the US Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)."
descriptionUrl: "https://hazards.fema.gov/nri/community-resilience"
domainIncludes: dcid:NaturalHazardImpact

# New unit: Fema Risk Index
Node: dcid:femaNaturalHazardRiskIndex
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "femaNaturalHazardRiskIndex"
description: "The potential for negative impacts as a result of a natural hazard. This is a measure defined and computed by the US Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)."
descriptionUrl: "https://hazards.fema.gov/nri/determining-risk"
domainIncludes: dcid:NaturalHazardImpact

### FEMA NRI-specific units
Node: dcid:FemaNationalRiskScore
typeOf: dcid:UnitOfMeasure
name: "FemaNationalRiskScore"
description: "A unit describing the relative risk from natural hazards that a place is estimated to be,according to the FEMA National Risk Index study. Ranging from 0 to 100,where 0 is the least at risk,and 100 is the most at risk. This is a relative scoring system defined and computed by the US Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA)."
shortDisplayName: "FNR score"
descriptionUrl: "https://hazards.fema.gov/nri/understanding-scores-ratings"

### FEMA NRI-specific population type
Node: dcid:NaturalHazardImpact
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:Intangible
name: "NaturalHazardImpact"
description: "Negative impacts,such as destruction or death,imposed upon factors such as Buildings,People,and Agriculture through occurrences of natural hazards."

Node: dcid:CMIP6ReferencePeriod
typeOf: dcid:QuantityRange
name: "CMIP6ReferencePeriod"
description: "The reference period used for comparison in IPCC CMIP6 report,which is from 1995 to 2014."
sameAs: [1995 2014 dcs:Date]

Node: dcid:heatWaveIntensity
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "heatWaveIntensity"
description: "Describes how hot the temperature is during heat waves. It is defined as the difference in temperature (measured in degrees Celsius) between the local threshold for heat waves and the average of the daily minimum temperature during the heat wave."
domainIncludes: dcid:HeatWaveEvent
rangeIncludes: dcid:Quantity

Node: dcid:vaporPressureDeficit
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "vaporPressureDeficit"
description: "The difference (deficit) between the amount of moisture in the air and how much moisture the air can hold when it is saturated."
descriptionUrl: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapour-pressure_deficit"
domainIncludes: dcid:Place
rangeIncludes: dcid:Quantity

