## Wet-Bulb Temperature Events
Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:TemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureEvent"
description: "A wet-bulb event happens when the estimated wet-bulb temperature (function of temperature and humidity) exceeds a threshold in Celsius."
descriptionUrl: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet-bulb_temperature"

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius31Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius31Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 31 degrees Celsius."

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius32Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius32Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 32 degrees Celsius."

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius33Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius33Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 33 degrees Celsius."

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius34Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius34Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 34 degrees Celsius."

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius35Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius35Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 35 degrees Celsius."

Node: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureCelsius36Event
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:WetBulbTemperatureEvent
name: "WetBulbTemperatureCelsius36Event"
description: "A wet-bulb event which happens when the wet bulb temperature exceeds 36 degrees Celsius."

## Temperature (Heat and Cold) Events
Node: dcid:TemperatureEvent
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:Event
name: "TemperatureEvent"
description: "A temperature event happens when the max/min temperature for a period (e.g. over a day) exceeds or is less than the reference (e.g. a long term average for the month) by a certain amount."

Node: dcid:HeatTemperatureEvent
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:TemperatureEvent
name: "HeatTemperatureEvent"
description: "A heat (temperature) event happens when the maximum temperature for a period (e.g. over a day) exceeds the reference (e.g. a long term average for the month) by a certain amount."

Node: dcid:ColdTemperatureEvent
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:TemperatureEvent
name: "ColdTemperatureEvent"
description: "A cold (temperature) event happens when the minimum temperature for a period (e.g. over a day) is below the reference (e.g. a long term average for the month) by a certain amount."

## Temperature Event properties
Node: dcid:temperatureDifference
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "temperatureDifference"
domainIncludes: dcid:TemperatureEvent,dcid:HeatTemperatureEvent,dcid:ColdTemperatureEvent
rangeIncludes: dcid:Quantity

Node: dcid:referenceTemperature
typeOf: dcid:Property
name: "referenceTemperature"
domainIncludes: dcid:TemperatureEvent,dcid:HeatTemperatureEvent,dcid:ColdTemperatureEvent
rangeIncludes: dcid:Quantity

