subClassOf: dcid:Place
name: "StateComponent"
description: "A state component is a portion of a state. For example,California -- Urban"

Node: dcid:CommutingZone
typeOf: dcid:Class
subClassOf: dcid:Place
name: "CommutingZone"
description: "A commuting zone is a geographic area used in population and economic analysis. For 1990,741 commuting zones were delineated for all U.S. counties and county equivalents. These commuting zones were developed without regard to a minimum population threshold and are intended to be a spatial measure of the local labor market."

Node: dcid:ElementarySchoolDistrict
